.TH Ncron "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
Ncron \- run commands at scheduled times
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/usr/lib/Ncron\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
Ncron -- run commands at scheduled times
Usage:	Ncron
Wakes up once a minute and runs every entry in '/usr/lib/crontab'
whose time fields match the current minute, hour, day of the month,
month, and day of the week; logs a note to '/usr/lib/cronlog' on
the hour and each time it runs a command.
No arguments and no options.
.HE
.B Ncron
reads the file
.B /usr/lib/crontab
and, once each minute, runs every entry in it whose time fields
match the current minute, hour, day of the month, month, and day of
the week.
.PP
At start-up
.B Ncron
sets its user and group id to those of user
.B daemon
if that user exists, changes its working directory to
.BR /bin ,
and arranges to wake up once every minute.
On each wakeup it rereads
.B /usr/lib/crontab
from the beginning, testing every entry; once every command it has
started has finished, it sleeps until the next minute.
.PP
Each line of
.B /usr/lib/crontab
has the form
.DS
	\fIminute hour month-day month week-day command\fR
.DE
The five time fields are separated by white space.
Each may be a single number, a range of two numbers separated by a
hyphen, a comma-separated list of numbers and/or ranges, or an
asterisk meaning every value of that field.
An entry runs only when the current time matches every one of its
five fields.
The
.I command
is the rest of the line and is passed to
.B popen
so that it runs under the shell.
A percent sign within
.I command
is turned into a newline, and everything following it is instead
fed to the command's standard input; a backslash escapes a literal
percent sign or continues the line onto the next.
.PP
.B Ncron
appends a line to
.B /usr/lib/cronlog
each time it starts a command, and, on the hour, a time stamp as
well.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 1.5i
	\fB/usr/lib/crontab\fR	table of scheduled commands
	\fB/usr/lib/cronlog\fR	log of commands run and hourly time stamps
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR at ,
.BR atrun ,
.B cron
.SH NOTES
.B Ncron
is a variant of the command
.B cron
found elsewhere in this source tree; the two differ only in that
.B Ncron
also writes an hourly time stamp, and each command it runs, to
.BR /usr/lib/cronlog .
There is no shipped binary built from this source in this tree; the
installed daemon is
.BR cron .
